# Katalyst Score Implemented

I have successfully added the Katalyst Scoring system to both the Student and Recruiter flows! 

## What changed?

### 1. The Core Scorer Engine
A new module `readyindex_scorer.py` is now in your backend. It handles fetching and calculating scores natively using your LeetCode and GitHub API snippets.

### 2. Live Re-Calculation
Added new API routes to `/api/students/{id}/katalyst-score`. When the student clicks "Recalculate" on their profile, it fetches fresh data directly from GitHub and LeetCode in real-time, stores the result, and breaks down the calculation.

### 3. Student Profile View
The student profile now features a **Katalyst Score Card** at the top next to the identity and resume buttons. It allows students to explicitly update and see their score out of 100 points, complete with a visual indicator and recalculation loading states.

### 4. Recruiter Talent Pool
The Recruiter Talent pool no longer shows a dummy `85% Match`! Instead, it pulls the actual `katalyst_score` generated for that specific student, allowing recruiters to make informed decisions about candidate proficiency.

---

> [!CAUTION]
> **Action Required: Run SQL Migration**
> To store these scores, you must run a quick SQL command in your Supabase SQL Editor. 
> I have saved this script as `supabase_migration.sql` in your project folder.
> 
> ```sql
> -- Add katalyst_score columns to student_profiles table
> ALTER TABLE public.student_profiles
> ADD COLUMN katalyst_score integer NULL,
> ADD COLUMN katalyst_score_breakdown jsonb NULL;
> ```

---

## How to Test
1. Run the SQL Migration in Supabase.
2. Go to your local frontend and view a Student Profile.
3. Add a valid `github_username` and `leetcode_username` to the profile.
4. Click **Recalculate** in the new Katalyst Score card!
5. Open the Talent Pool view and notice the updated scores.
